{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And the waters, etc.</b> ״וְהָיוּ״ ״וְהָיוּ״ — two times it appears to me [superfluous]. Had it been said וְהָיוּ הַמַּיִם אֲשֶׁר תִּקַּח מִן הַיְאוֹר לְדָם בַּיַּבָּשֶׁת, I would understand that they turn to blood in his hand — and even when they fall to the ground they would remain as they are; but now it teaches us that they would not be blood until they are on the dry ground."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:50:29.298867356Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}